WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- What do you say?

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.300
I mean I try to educate my
children as much as I can

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.670
with the age appropriate
information obviously.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.560
But you try, and it's
like some things are like,

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.180
God, I can't believe I have
to have this conversation

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.013
with my kid.

00:00:12.013 --> 00:00:13.410
- Yeah, absolutely
- I can't imagine

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.580
you having to tell your boy, like hey,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:16.420
this is how it is.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.940
Like, that's not what you
want to tell your kid.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.200
- Yeah, I tell my son all the time,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.740
man, it's not a good conversation
but it has to be had.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.640
I just always tell him, man,

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.470
police ever mess with you or whatever,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.300
just do what they say.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.750
You know, and that's it.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.610
I mean you're right.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.580
You have the right to say
and do whatever you want to,

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.270
but realistically we
want you to come home.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.400
Just comply.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.540
Do what you gotta do.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.373
And come home.

00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:42.440
Don't say nothing.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.490
Say the least that you have to say.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.380
And that's it.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.410
And they might be doing wrong to him,

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:50.052
I still tell him just do what he has to do

00:00:50.052 --> 00:00:52.220
or whatever in order to come home.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.250
Because there's a lot of
heroes that aren't here.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.083
You know.

00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:58.256
And so, I mean, I want him to stand up

00:00:58.256 --> 00:01:00.710
for how he feels or whatever,

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.610
but when he's by his self

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.490
at night, and there's
four police officers,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.910
I need for you to come home.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.431
And then you come get me,

00:01:08.431 --> 00:01:10.287
and we go deal with it.

00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:11.920
You know, and so I have to let him know

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.120
to just do what he gotta do

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.050
in order to get back to me basically.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.530
- I'm sorry you even have
to have that conversation.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.900
- Yeah, but it's like I
said, it's a conversation

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.796
that's been going on for all our lives.

00:01:22.796 --> 00:01:26.260
My uncles, and my grandfather taught me

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:30.032
and I'm quite sure they
uncles and they grandfathers

00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:32.673
taught them, so it's
just this mentality that

00:01:32.673 --> 00:01:35.290
goes down and goes down or whatever.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:36.250
But I tell you this much,

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.720
white people nice as hell lately boy, woo.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.860
They been nice as hell.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.119
I was at the grocery store
and I had 2 customer services.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:45.396
(laughter)
I was like this is.

00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:47.530
(laughter)

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.845
I was like this is all right.

00:01:48.845 --> 00:01:50.030
Boy, I like this.

